  "note": "The executable half of the knowledge base. Prose cards give an underwriter context; these typed rules are what actually routes a case, so they can be reviewed, diffed and tested one by one. Every rule cites the card it came from. Thresholds are demonstration settings, not underwriting policy. No rule can accept or decline: the only actions are refer, request_evidence and note.",
  "comparison_semantics": "Mirrors demo/governance.py: a blocking rule whose field is missing or out of catalogue range produces an evidence request rather than being skipped.",
